<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Konstantin Päts</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1874–1956</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Konstantin Päts was an Estonian journalist and politician who headed the Provincial Government of 1917 and the provisional government of the new Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> in 1918, during the War of Independence. He served several times as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-elder">State Elder</a>, and in 1934 he and General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johan-laidoner">Johan Laidoner</a> staged a coup and ruled by decree. He became president in 1938, was deported by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> in 1940 and died in a Soviet psychiatric hospital in 1956.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/konstantin-pats.jpg" alt="Konstantin Päts" width="320" height="503" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Konstantin_P%C3%A4ts.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
